          "source": "wotc",
          "published_at": "2004-12-01",
          "comment": "The permanents have to share a permanent type both when the target is chosen and when the ability resolves."
        },
        {
          "object": "ruling",
          "oracle_id": "e477abb9-9b99-48a8-8c09-07b120b72540",
          "source": "wotc",
          "published_at": "2004-12-01",
          "comment": "Even though Confusion in the Ranks triggers only when an artifact, creature, or enchantment enters, the ability can target a land if the permanent entering is an artifact land."
        },
        {
          "object": "ruling",
          "oracle_id": "e477abb9-9b99-48a8-8c09-07b120b72540",
          "source": "wotc",
          "published_at": "2004-12-01",
          "comment": "The permanents are exchanged only if they're both on the battlefield when the ability resolves."
        },
        {
          "object": "ruling",
          "oracle_id": "e477abb9-9b99-48a8-8c09-07b120b72540",
          "source": "wotc",
          "published_at": "2004-12-01",
          "comment": "Confusion in the Ranks triggers on itself entering. If an opponent controls an enchantment, exchange Confusion in the Ranks for that enchantment."
        },
        {
          "object": "ruling",
          "oracle_id": "e477abb9-9b99-48a8-8c09-07b120b72540",
          "source": "wotc",
          "published_at": "2004-10-04",
          "comment": "The exchange isn't optional. If there is a legal choice, you must make one."
        }
      ]
    }
